  "checks": [
    "D3D8 and D3D9 retain per-buffer processed clip records when CLIPPING is enabled during ProcessVertices",
    "ordinary and indexed draws share the existing homogeneous clipping kernel; draw-time CLIPPING changes do not discard processing records",
    "byte-addressed positions preserve nonzero source/destination indices, D3D9 source/draw stream offsets and output declaration POSITIONT offsets",
    "indexed draws validate MinVertexIndex as well as the upper bound, signed D3D9 base indices and nonzero StartIndex; D3D8 exercises 16/32-bit indices",
    "internal draw emission preserves application VB/IB bindings across successive calls",
    "shared Windows scratch allocation replaces D3D7-only allocation; DISCARD and VB release free processing records",
    "zero guard-band caps select viewport boundaries; D3D9 permissive advertised guard bands still use caps",
    "D3D8 snapshots aliased ProcessVertices input, matching the existing D3D9 rule",
    "public traces contain only procedural draw data; unrelated cursor/texture bytes and diagnostic text are zeroed"
  ],
  "scope": "Frustum clipping integration for supported fixed-function, single-stream processed layouts in D3D7/8/9. The original Microsoft D3D7 storage/raster reference remains independent; this stage does not claim native Microsoft D3D8/9 or full Wine/game equivalence. User planes, general packed/output/multistream layouts and programmable processing continue next. Raw direct zero-W backend interpolation remains diagnostic.",
